# Forms & Paginated Lists

Most game UIs use fixed enums (no pagination). When adding **forms** or **large/remote lists**, follow these standards so the codebase stays consistent.

## Paginated data lists

- BLoC state: `hasMore` + `items` (or equivalent).
- `loadMore` uses `offset: state.items.length`; refresh resets to offset `0`.
- UI: `NotificationListener<ScrollNotification>` near bottom to load more.
- `RefreshIndicator` for pull-to-refresh.
- Bottom loader / skeleton while fetching next page; inline retry on failure.

Fixed catalogs (`CellId`, `ResearchMaterialId`, research tree) may render fully without pagination.

## Forms

- Layout: `CustomScrollView` + `SliverPadding` + `SliverList.list` preferred.
- While processing: inputs `readOnly: true`; primary button shows loading.
- Status / failure text directly above the submit button.
- Validation errors hidden until submit (or explicit invalid).
- All strings via `context.l10n`.
- Prefer shared field widgets (`AmountTextField` today; add themed text fields as needed rather than one-offs).
